            <ArticleTitle>[Pharmacology of azidomorphine].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>685-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As revealed, in acute experiments on rabbits, cats, and rats, a new morphine-like synthetic analgesic drug azidomorphine exceeded 20--100-fold the morphine ability to inhibit synaptic transmission in the thalamic structures, cerebral cortex, and the spinal cord during the nociceptive stimulation, and also by its analgesic activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
